  "title": "Lothal (Harappan site, Gujarat)",
  "summary": "Lothal is a Harappan (Indus civilization) site in the Bhal region of Gujarat, near the Gulf of Khambhat. S. R. Rao of the Archaeological Survey of India excavated it from 1955 to 1960. A large brick basin there was read by Rao as a tidal dock, while Lawrence Leshnik argued it was more likely an irrigation tank, so its function is debated.",
